1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,803
Two guilty men were dying beside Jesus, with

2
00:00:02,904 --> 00:00:04,532
no time left to fix anything.

3
00:00:04,708 --> 00:00:05,309
Both guilty.

4
00:00:05,869 --> 00:00:06,829
Both just as close.

5
00:00:07,589 --> 00:00:08,309
Both spoke.

6
00:00:08,909 --> 00:00:11,750
If thou be Christ, save thyself and us.

7
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:13,730
A taunt, not a prayer.

8
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:15,110
The other thief rebuked him.

9
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:18,971
And we indeed justly; for we receive the due

10
00:00:19,031 --> 00:00:22,292
reward of our deeds: but this man hath done

11
00:00:22,432 --> 00:00:23,352
nothing amiss.

12
00:00:23,632 --> 00:00:24,232
A confession.

13
00:00:25,012 --> 00:00:26,452
A verdict: innocent.

14
00:00:27,473 --> 00:00:28,273
Then one request.

15
00:00:28,873 --> 00:00:32,273
Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy

16
00:00:32,313 --> 00:00:32,693
kingdom.

17
00:00:33,234 --> 00:00:37,514
Verily I say unto thee, To day shalt thou be

18
00:00:37,554 --> 00:00:39,475
with me in paradise.

19
00:00:39,675 --> 00:00:40,595
He asked for someday.

20
00:00:41,515 --> 00:00:43,075
Jesus gave him that same afternoon.

21
00:00:43,215 --> 00:00:43,715
No merit.

22
00:00:44,156 --> 00:00:45,516
Just repentance and trust.

23
00:00:45,636 --> 00:00:47,176
We are all one of those two men.

24
00:00:47,376 --> 00:00:48,436
Ask what the thief asked.

25
00:00:49,156 --> 00:00:49,676
Remember me.

26
00:00:50,817 --> 00:00:51,597
Then hear his answer.

27
00:00:52,737 --> 00:00:53,097
With me.

28
00:00:53,957 --> 00:00:54,297
Today.

29
00:00:55,398 --> 00:00:55,838
Paradise.
